          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. If we multiply a number by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 5 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and add "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{2}{3}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to the product, we get "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\frac { - 7 } { 1 2 } } ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Find the number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.173,
            0.886,
            0.235
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. A positive number is 5 times another number. If 21 is added to both the numbers, then one of the new numbers becomes twice the other new number. What are the numbers?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.242,
            0.886,
            0.304
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. If you have `800 and you save `250 every month, find the amount you have after (i) 6 months (ii) 2 years. Express this as a linear pattern."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.31,
            0.886,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*6. The digits of a two-digit number differ by 3. If the digits are interchanged, and the resulting number is added to the original number, we get 143. Find both the numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
